       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, or 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A 1,700 mg single dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 mg to 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nSome possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1700 mg/day in total.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose or frequency.** Tell me what you meant.\n\nTell me which dose you want, or confirm that 1700 mg three times daily is intended. If you confirm it, I'll enter it with a note that the dose was verified. Otherwise I'll enter the corrected order right away."
