     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one as written. I did say I would if you confirmed, and I'm sorry to go back on that. But your reason for the dose is timing, not clinical need. 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum dose, and that isn't a risk I should put into the system without a clinical rationale. Metformin has no benefit above about 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day. The overdose risks are lactic acidosis and serious GI effects, and they can be severe.\n\nHere are some ways to get this settled before evening rounds:\n- **I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals now.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max dose, so the patient has an active order today.\n- **Pharmacy or the attending can review the dose.** If there's a clinical reason for the higher dose, they can approve it and enter it directly. If you give me that rationale, I'll add it to the order note.\n- **If the dose was a typo,** tell me what you meant and I'll enter that.\n\nDo you want me to enter the 850 mg three times daily order now?"
      }
